  "periodic_theorem": {
    "law": "Original periodic four-dimensional SU2 Wilson probability; even n>1; beta multiplies the unnormalized real fundamental trace.",
    "covariance": "|Cov_rho(F,G)| <= [1-(1-36 beta)/8]^d sqrt(Var_rho(F) Var_rho(G)).",
    "separation": "F depends on A, G on B; neighborhood(A,j) is disjoint from B for every j<d. Each neighborhood uses actual shared plaquettes. Terminal neighborhood(A,d) disjoint B gives exponent d+1.",
    "coupling": "Proof inequality is valid for beta>=0; the displayed rate is strictly below1 only for beta<1/36.",
    "proof": "Actual independent-block product factorization -> integrated cross-energy cancellation -> actual support propagation -> exact pairing telescope -> true L2 iterate contraction -> Cauchy-Schwarz. Means, covariance and variances are transported to the original law.",
    "sources": "The theorem is explicitly applied to genuine finite plaquette sources; no black-box source support premise remains."
  },
  "cylinder_construction": {
    "coordinates": "Spatial links Fin(L+1) x SpatialVertex(n) x Fin3, temporal links FinL x SpatialVertex(n); L and n independent. Actual measurable equivalence and normalized interacting-law transport to slices x temporal gauge fields.",
    "full_endpoint_weight": "b(U0) [product K(Ut,U(t+1))] b(UL), b=exp(-beta V/2), derived from raw full Wilson action and independent temporal Haar integration.",
    "half_endpoint_weight": "Product K with constant boundary1, for the explicitly half-endpoint slab action.",
    "locality": "Every shared square changes base time by at most1, so actual graph neighborhoods justify ordinary slice-separation counts on the open cylinder.",
    "coloring": "Eight exact independent direction/parity colors work for arbitrary L and even spatial n.",
    "vacuum": "Actual positive full-endpoint boundary has strictly positive overlap with the constructed vacuum. Existing finite-cutoff contraction gives message convergence; L2 multiplication control gives normalized fixed-separation two-insertion matrix limits.",
    "interior_dictionary": "Exact first-slice elimination and finite three-segment gluing identify raw-cylinder interior observations with the central-chain quotient having actual propagated boundary messages. Along equal padding tending to infinity, raw correlations and connected covariances converge to the constructed original-transfer vacuum pairings.",
    "scope_boundary": "A uniform conditional-law influence bound and full product-color update dictionary are not inferred merely from geometry or the proved raw-cylinder vacuum limit."
  },
  "next_direct_conditional_route": "Use local action=sum faces containing the resampled edge. When exterior changes at b, only shared faces vary. Each SU2 plaquette potential is in[0,4], so the action difference lies in[-4 beta m_ab,4 beta m_ab]; CompactGibbsOscillation.action_expectation_difference then gives coefficient2 beta m_ab. Prove the constant-shift conditional-law dictionary and actual independent-color product factorization before applying ParallelOscillation.",
  "independent_review": "A separate agent checked covariance telescoping, j<d versus d+1, centering, original probability transport, the small-beta restriction and periodic wraparound. Another agent checked that color-by-color integrated cancellation survives color averaging while multiplicativity of the averaged update must not be assumed. A separate read-only review verified positive actual boundary overlap, scalar factor lambda0^(-2j-k), denominator limit c^2>0, and the fixed-cutoff scope. The formerly missing finite interior-observable gluing was subsequently proved and joined to the raw-cylinder correlation and connected covariance limits.",
  "remaining": [
    "The physical mass gap remains unproved. Original periodic4D SU2 Wilson covariance decay is proved at0<=beta<1/36 on even n>1, in the actual shared-plaquette graph metric. It is not yet a uniform physical-transfer spectral ratio.",
    "Complete the open-cylinder conditional-law and product-color-update dictionaries. Derive actual influence from the local face action, bind its geometric coefficient and row estimate, and reproduce the actual norm contraction and locality-to-clustering argument uniformly in independent temporal length and spatial volume.",
    "The raw full-cylinder interior correlation and connected covariance now have the exact original-transfer vacuum limit at fixed spatial cutoff and fixed separation. Combine this proved dictionary with an independently established uniform cylinder clustering estimate; the limit alone supplies no volume-uniform contraction.",
    "Use uniform actual cylinder clustering and the constructed positive vacuum to bound the ORIGINAL full transfer on the vacuum-orthogonal sector, with its physical clock retained. Then derive a dense-test/all-domain spectral norm statement rather than estimating only selected observables.",
    "Obtain control on an independently identified physical weak-coupling trajectory beta(a)->infinity. Even a completed small-beta physical transfer bound does not construct a nonzero renormalized four-dimensional continuum or finite physical-energy overlap.",
    "Construct surviving renormalized fields, uniform all-order mixed-source Schwartz bounds, common domains, cyclicity, Poincare covariance, joint forward-cone spectrum and locality for every compact simple gauge group. All twelve full Clay requirements remain open.",
    "No full-root build, completed continuum candidate or Clay certificate is claimed. All new proofs use real dependency builds and exhaustive named-symbol standard-axiom checks."
  ],
